comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T15:03:08.302Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before create: read pm-fs8q9x (flags), pm-wt43zj (nouns/verbs), pm-hqa8g1 (exit codes), pm-x4nn3z (error codes), pm-pbyu (noun-verb ADR), pm-7i97c3 (command intent), pm-gy885b (closed value domains) in full. All four grammar-governance items scope explicitly to flags, nouns/verbs, exit codes, and error codes respectively; none mentions positional arguments in title, description, or AC. pm-gy885b covers value domains a refusal fails to name, which is adjacent but concerns flag VALUES, not slot arity - recorded as discovered_from. No existing n7rr child covers argument placement; the existing children all consolidate which commands exist, not how their arguments are shaped."
  "2026-08-07T17:13:34.757Z","harness:claude-code","Another instance of the subcommand-scoped positional requirement, found while measuring graph analytics 2026-08-07. `pm graph dominators --json` exits 2 with \"graph dominators requires an item id\" under code invalid_argument_value. It is a correct refusal and it is invisible from the declared arity: `pm graph --help` renders the id positional as \"Root item id (traversals, paths, impact, and dominators)\", so the requirement is carried in prose inside an argument description rather than in the grammar. Of the sixteen graph subcommands, four require the id positional, one requires a second target positional, and eleven take none, all under a single declared `[id] [target]` shape. This is the same class as the schema/profile/plan versus graph/merge divergence already recorded here: one command, several arities, and the arity a caller must satisfy is discoverable only by being refused."
  "2026-08-18T04:51:46.250Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-18: one coupled SDK/CLI/MCP tranche will make positional actions and recovery references contract-declared, executable, parity-gated, and discoverable. Scope includes generated contracts, public SDK types, CLI help and recovery, MCP aliases, assurance negative controls, documentation, temporary-workspace acceptance, and packed npm/Bun consumers. Duplicate check used the complete 2,521-item all-status corpus with zero omissions or truncation."
  "2026-08-18T06:29:31.904Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: positional grammar gate reports 158 declared and 158 observed executable destinations, 20 distinct positional shapes under the budget of 21, no inactive package omissions, and zero findings. Full literal coverage passed 7,540 tests at 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-18T06:45:41.690Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: the public grammar table declares 158 observed/158 declared destinations with zero findings, 20 positional shapes under the budget of 21, typed required/variadic/value-kind semantics, public SDK exports, and a persistent-regression negative control. PM-linked focused execution passed 13/13 tests; full coverage and the repository grammar gate passed."
  "2026-08-18T07:33:26.415Z","harness:codex","Review verification before close: duplicate declared and observed signatures now fail deterministically; an active package summary missing its signature fails while an inactive package signature is retained exactly once; assurance apply help is executable. Focused 18/18 and full 7,542/7,542 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100; live grammar gate is 158/158 with 20/21 shapes and zero findings."
  "2026-08-18T08:04:17.664Z","harness:codex","Independent review start: removed temporary software-delivery preset artifacts whose example owner pm-a1b2 does not exist; harden descriptions, canonical signature identity, explicit-slot census integrity, and generated changelog linkage."
  "2026-08-18T08:53:10.637Z","harness:codex","Final independent-review evidence: explicit-slot orphan census, duplicate destination/signature detection, key-order-independent canonical identity, generated descriptions, and a non-mutating <pm-item-id> assurance example are covered. Exact coverage passed 519 files / 7,543 tests at 100/100/100/100; pnpm lint, grammar 158/158 with 20/21 shapes, contracts, SDK surface, token gates, graph/record assurance, and six-operation transport floor all pass."
  "2026-08-18T09:13:43.788Z","harness:codex","Hosted exact-head evidence: CI run 32119085781 job 95655444284 reproduced locally in a fresh temporary project with search-advanced active; contracts --summary --json is 24,845 bytes and contracts --json is 24,719 versus budgets 17,352/17,213. Cause: 27 virtual action paths are already present in compact grammar_contracts but are redundantly expanded into per-command summaries."
  "2026-08-18T10:02:39.974Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 519 files / 7,545 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100; contracts and SDK snapshots are current; 32 answer budgets, 72 package-active discovery surfaces, graph 7/7, record integrity 1/1, and changelog check pass. Exact-head hosted timing gates will revalidate the unchanged performance budgets after push."
  "2026-08-18T10:45:41.996Z","harness:codex","Hosted exact-head timing evidence: PR #1059 run 32126787587 at head 4281343f3 passed Gates (smokes), Gates (static), Run benchmarks, all four coverage shards, aggregate coverage, and Codecov patch. This supersedes the earlier failing 24,845/24,719-byte measurement; the corrected search-active contract surface passed its committed budgets before the item is reclosed."
  "2026-08-18T10:56:53.765Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: the late-review normalization and help-formatting changes passed ESLint, zero-clone duplicate detection, the focused 89-test contract suite, contracts:check, sdk:surface:check, the 158-destination positional grammar gate, the 43-create/48-update MCP parity gate, the 32-surface token budget gate, the isolated search-active 99-surface agent token ratchet, defect-evidence validation, graph and record assurance, and full repository coverage at exactly 53,124/53,124 lines, 55,035/55,035 statements, 11,369/11,369 functions, and 41,062/41,062 branches. The hosted exact-head run for 4281343f3 also passed all required static, smoke, compatibility, shard, aggregate coverage, benchmark, security, Codecov, Windows, and CodeQL gates."
  "2026-08-18T12:13:59.674Z","harness:codex","Evidence: injected positional declaration verification is now isolated from the repository-global explicit-slot census, while the default governed verification still executes that census. Regression coverage now selects plan reorder-step so whitespace normalization and slot reorder checks exercise a multi-token, multi-slot signature rather than a vacuous item command. Focused grammar suite and command-grammar gate passed with 158 declared/observed commands and zero findings."
  "2026-08-18T14:49:46.350Z","harness:codex","Terminal local evidence: the independent structured-help/runtime census reports 166 observed of 166 declared destinations, 32 typed positional actions, 20/21 shapes, 61 visible top-level commands under the 69 ceiling, zero findings, and MCP parity at 43 create / 48 update parameters. Focused regression coverage passes; full repository execution passes 521 files / 7,557 tests at exact 55,127/55,127 statements, 41,148/41,148 branches, 11,394/11,394 functions, and 53,208/53,208 lines. A packed 2026.8.18 tarball passed isolated npx, Bun, and bunx help/initialization acceptance."
  "2026-08-18T15:07:12.068Z","harness:codex","Hosted smoke diagnosis: run 32151583809 proved context assurance passed but correctly failed discovery governance because the five newly executable workspace snapshot action paths lacked committed token-surface rows. Regenerated the baseline from the built CLI; the independent surface now covers 112 ratchets and pnpm quality:token-surface passes. This is generated contract evidence, not a relaxed ceiling."
  "2026-08-18T15:19:20.024Z","harness:codex","Late review fix: alias expansion now rejects alias paths whose token arity differs from the canonical path, which prevents unbounded Set growth while preserving the transitive equal-arity expansion required for package/packages lifecycle aliases. A longer-alias regression terminates with the expected missing destination; focused script coverage remains exact 100/100/100/100, the real census remains 166/166, and the 112-surface token ratchet passes."
  "2026-08-18T15:33:42.903Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence 2026-08-18 at PR #1059 head bec9a1b3b: command membership is independently observed, but positional slot rows are still read from grammar_contracts.positional_signatures. The gate therefore cannot detect a runtime Commander arity change unless live structured-help/runtime action views independently contribute slot shape. Repair will add that independent observation and a negative control."
  "2026-08-18T16:34:53.995Z","harness:codex","Final recurrence repair evidence: the command grammar gate now derives positional names, requiredness, and variadicity from live structured Commander help and runtime action views rather than the declared positional table. The negative control detects live arity drift; malformed help, absent active-package help, no-slot alias expansion, and both empty-signature mismatch directions are covered. The live gate reports 166 observed/166 declared, 20/21 positional shapes, 61/69 visible top-level commands, zero findings, and MCP parity. Rich plan/schema/profile recovery remains intact across 183 focused tests; full exact coverage and packed npm/Bun acceptance pass."
  "2026-08-18T17:12:13.213Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review repair evidence: CodeRabbit threads 3806115371, 3806115380, 3806115412, and 3806115421 were reproduced and fixed. Active-package help read failures now become structured fail-closed findings; missing positional-action destination rows are part of the positional census; action help resolves the longest declared path before positional operands; action descriptions are explicit. Live pm help plan add-step pm-a1b2 resolves to plan add-step with its typed plan-id and applicable flags. Focused 32/32 tests pass, pnpm lint passes with zero clones and 100% docstrings, grammar remains 166/166 with 20/21 shapes, full 521-file / 7,562-test coverage is exactly 55,170/55,170 statements, 41,190/41,190 branches, 11,407/11,407 functions, and 53,252/53,252 lines, and exact-diff Bugbot reports no findings."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-18T08:53:09.987Z","harness:codex","Exact positional identity and shape budgeting are separate invariants: exact comparison must include slot names, while the bounded shape key intentionally excludes names so semantic arity vocabulary remains stable."
  "2026-08-18T10:02:39.030Z","harness:codex","Default compact discovery and targeted recovery should be asymmetric: omit repeated detail across the whole command catalog, but preserve exact detail when a command is explicitly selected so gates and agents do not infer the wrong format contract."
